Stop a large diff -U from overflowing the hunk arithmetic.
diff() computes 2 * context + 1 to decide whether two changes share a
hunk, and adds the context to line numbers for the hunk ranges, all in
int. A context of 2^30 or more overflowed: every change got a hunk of
its own, so the hunks overlapped and repeated lines, and near 2^31 the
ranges in the @@ lines went negative. A context larger than the number
of lines changes nothing, so clamp it to INT_MAX / 4 after parsing.

---
 editors/diff.c |    4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

--- a/editors/diff.c
+++ b/editors/diff.c
@@ -1043,6 +1043,10 @@
 			LONGOPTS,
 			&L_arg, &s_start, &opt_U_context);
 	argv += optind;
+	/* More context than lines changes nothing; keep line + 2 * context
+	 * from overflowing in diff() */
+	if (opt_U_context > INT_MAX / 4)
+		opt_U_context = INT_MAX / 4;
 	while (L_arg)
 		label[!!label[0]] = llist_pop(&L_arg);
 
